Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 29 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSIES  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED   SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  NOTE  The tumor is present in all cores  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 43                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are multiple fragments of core biopsies up to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Submitted in cassette A  Resident  GARY LETTS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Angela Ann Giardino  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY   report_end  , 1.
