s dissected to reveal multiple rubbery lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Representative sections of the fibrocystic areas are submitted in A J with lymph nodes in K M  M contains one bisected node  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast modified radical   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm modified radical mastectomy with REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm axillary tail  with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm wrinkled tan skin ellipse containing a 3 0cm tan areola  with a central 1 1cm everted tan nipple  The specimen is oriented by 1 short suture denoting superior  1 long suture denoting lateral  The specimen is black inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm indurated gritty tan white slightly ill defined bilobed tumor  which has a narrow fibrous extension between the two masses  This tumor is within 0 1cm of the posterior margin  within 0 1cm of the superior anterior margin  4 0cm from the lateral margin and 0 4cm from the anterior interior margin  The remaining parenchyma is approximately 80  dense  multicystic and focally indurated fibrous tissue with cysts ranging to 1 4cm in greatest dimension  admixed with approximately 20  tan lobular fat  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple rubbery lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows  N  tumor to posterior margin  O  tumor to anterior superior margin  P  tumor to inferior margin  Q  tumor to posterior margin  R  representative sections of fibroglandular tissue away from tumor  S AA  Axillary lymph nodes  Please note Y and Z contain each 1 bisected node   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  highest right axillary lymph   and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan yellow lobular portion of